  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIDSE/CI Task Group 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.  To continue the Jubilee call for cancellation of poor countries&apos; unpayable debts, especially by urging that debt relief be expanded to non-HIPC countries, and to provide a level of debt reduction that is based on a country&apos;s human development needs.
2.  To monitor the implementation of the expanded Heavily Indebted Poor Country Initiative (HIPC) in order to ensure that creditor governments and institutions at least fulfill their pledges and that debt reduction directly benefits poor people.
3.  To urge officials and political leaders in developing country governments as well as those in donor/creditor governments and international lending institutions to adopt poverty reduction as a central goal in national economic policy and programs.
4.  To stimulate and support the role of civil society organisations, especially the Catholic Church, as advocates for poverty reduction in decision-making at national and international forums, including through the Poverty Reduction Strategy initiative of the World Bank and IMF.
5.  To promote processes and structures that establish fairer relationships between debtors and creditors on the resolution of debt problems, and to prevent the recurrence of future debt crises.</narrative>
  </description>
